.TH SIFT 1 "August 2026" "sift 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sift \- automated, safety-first disk reclamation for macOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sift
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sift
identifies reclaimable disk space, attributes it to a named source, and
reclaims it reversibly on a schedule. It runs as the invoking user, makes no
network connections, and deletes nothing without an explicit
.BR clean .
.PP
A path becomes a deletion candidate only because a specific scanner claimed it
by an explicit rule. There is no mode that scans the whole disk and excludes
what it believes to be dangerous.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Report reclaimable space. Deletes nothing. This is the default.
.TP
.B clean
Scan, then move candidates to quarantine. Prompts unless
.BR \-\-yes .
Destructive scanners require typing the scanner's name regardless.
.TP
.B purge
Hard-delete quarantined items past their TTL.
.B \-\-now
ignores the TTL.
.TP
.BI restore " RUN_ID"
Return a quarantined run to its original locations. A unique prefix suffices.
Refuses rather than overwrites an occupied destination.
.TP
.B report
Show the last run, what is currently quarantined, and a trend.
.TP
.B doctor
Report permissions, tool availability, and per-scanner status with remediation.
.TP
.BI explain " PATH"
Describe a path, what deleting it would cost, and whether any scanner could
ever claim it. Deletes nothing.
.TP
.B install
Install the scheduled LaunchAgent.
.B \-\-dry\-run
shows the plist and launchctl command without executing either.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove the agent, plist, quarantine, and configuration. Retains the run history
and prints its path.
.TP
.B config check
Validate the configuration and print the effective merged values with sources.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON. Logging goes to stderr, so stdout stays parseable.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Use an alternate configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
For
.BR clean ", report what would happen and do nothing."
.TP
.B \-\-estimate\-delegated
Ask delegated tools how much they would reclaim. Without it those lines report
.BR unknown ,
not a size, and are excluded from the run total. Off by default: it spawns
subprocesses and lets them create their own cache directories.
.IP
Only some tools can answer.
.BR brew ", " docker " and " simctl
report what they hold;
.BR uv ", " pnpm ", " yarn " and " cargo\-sweep
have no dry\-run and no reporting mode, so those lines stay
.B unknown
regardless. The report distinguishes the two rather than implying the flag
would help.
.TP
.B \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the crate version, the commit it was built from, and the build date, as
.BR "sift 0.1.0 (d6c302d, built 2026-08-02)" .
A
.B \-dirty
suffix means the working tree had uncommitted changes. The commit is omitted
when the source is not a git checkout. Builds honour
.BR SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH .
.TP
.B \-\-include\-disabled
For
.BR scan ", also report scanners switched off in config, in a separate block"
excluded from the run total.
.B clean
ignores them regardless, and this option does not exist on it. Overrides the
.B enabled
switch only; a scanner above
.B max_risk
stays unrun.
.TP
.BI \-\-only " GLOB"
Restrict to scanners matching a glob, e.g. \fBxcode-*\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including a gated no-op scheduled run.
.TP
.B 1
Unhandled runtime error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid configuration.
.TP
.B 3
Required permission unavailable and no scanners could run.
.TP
.B 4
Circuit breaker tripped. Nothing was actioned.
.TP
.B 5
Completed with one or more scanner errors.
.TP
.B 64
CLI usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sift/config.toml
Configuration. Absence means all defaults.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/sift/quarantine/
Staged deletions, one directory per run.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/sift/history.jsonl
One JSON record per run. Retained by
.BR uninstall .
.TP
.I ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.cindral.sift.plist
The scheduled agent.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SIFT_LOG
Log filter, e.g.
.BR sift=debug .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME
Honoured when set to absolute paths.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation in the
.I docs/
directory of the source tree.
